    Call 1: ('In libjxl/lib/jxl/icc_codec.cc, what safe/fallible varint decoding API is available in this repository that can guarantee a varint is fully contained within a specified byte range such as commands_end? Please provide definitions/signatures and representative callers. Also explain DecodeVarInt behavior on truncated input.', "I am fixing the reported 32-bit heap OOB in UnpredictICC at libjxl/lib/jxl/icc_codec.cc:279-287. The function currently calls DecodeVarInt(enc, size, &cpos) for command-stream values even though commands_end may be less than size, allowing a malformed varint to consume data-stream bytes. Predict's uint64_t num is then implicitly narrowed by CheckOutOfBounds and PaddedBytes allocation on 32-bit, while loops retain the uint64_t comparison. Similar command-stream calls exist for numtags, tag offsets/sizes, Insert count, Shuffle count, Predict stride/count. I need the idiomatic root-cause fix, likely a checked decoder bounded by commands_end plus CheckIs32Bit before size_t use.")...
